  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1156 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nZonal flow across the northern plains continues through the \nweek with transient shortwave activity. The axis of greatest \ninstability looks to mainly stay south of the area keeping only \ngeneral thunderstorm chances for our forecast area, but cant \nrule out some strong to severe storms through the period. As the\nHudson Bay low begins to break down later in the week by \nThursday, Montana/Western ND ridging amplifies with decent \nlatitudinal differences among cluster analysis and degrading \nsynoptic flow agreement overall by Friday. Scenarios range from\nriding over the area to SW flow or zonal/WNW flow flow across \nthe Canadian prairies and northern plains. While the confidence\nin the long term evolution of the pattern is shaky the chance \nfor significant weather impacts through next weekend still \nappears low even with a spread in models.\n\nBest chance in the near term for impacts will be via \nthunderstorms Monday and Tuesday, but overall the environment \nis not terribly concerning from a severe perspective. Maybe just\nsome heavy rain and lightning with gusty winds and small hail. \nPer cluster analysis chances for greater than 0.10\" are 40% or \nless for any given spot in a 24 hour period through Thursday. \nPrecip chances look to increase for next weekend but that will \ndepend on the how the synoptic pattern unfolds.",
